SketchMind: Toward Executable Pen-Based 
Sketching for Constructing Sorting Algorithms

0:00:05.040,0:00:08.240
When learning algorithms, we often 
trace them with pen and paper,

0:00:08.240,0:00:12.880
but these traces can get long and go wrong.
SketchMind turns learners’ sketches into

0:00:12.880,0:00:16.640
executable plans. Users can draw 
free-form strokes to perform

0:00:16.640,0:00:21.840
operations. The system keeps a replayable 
record of the learner’s reasoning process.

0:00:21.840,0:00:27.680
SketchMind provides counterexamples as feedback 
to help learners identify and fix their plans.

0:00:27.680,0:00:29.537
